@* Wendy's: Competitive Activities, a project in the Marketing carousel (rendered from _MarketingWork.cshtml).
   Built from my one-page competitive activities map: Wendy's core position, the activities that hold it up today (red)
   and six new ones I proposed (blue). Every number and name here is from that slide. The full map is in the archive under the slideshow.
   The look: Wendy's red on a blush background, with my proposals in blue. The cover video is a motion graphic I made
   (tools/record/wendys-cover.html): a Dave's Single falling into place, layer by layer, around its square patty. *@
<style>
    .mk-wd { --w-red: #C8102E; --w-deep: #A50E26; --w-blue: #2F86D0; --w-bluedeep: #1F6FB5; --w-blush: #FCEFEF; --w-ink: #2A1810; --w-mute: #6E5A55; --w-cheese: #F2C94C; }
    .mk-wd .mk-stage { background: radial-gradient(34cqw 26cqw at 100% 0%, rgba(200, 16, 46, 0.12), rgba(200, 16, 46, 0)), radial-gradient(30cqw 24cqw at 0% 100%, rgba(47, 134, 208, 0.1), rgba(47, 134, 208, 0)), var(--w-blush); border: 1px solid #F1D2D2; }
    .mk-wd .mk-slide { color: var(--w-ink); padding: 3.4cqw 4.6cqw 3cqw; gap: 1.4cqw; }
    .mk-wd .mk-slide p { color: var(--w-mute); }
    .mk-wd .w-kick { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(9px, 0.95cqw, 12px) !important; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.2cqw; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--w-red) !important; }
    .mk-wd .w-kick.blue { color: var(--w-blue) !important; }
    .mk-wd .w-h { margin: 0; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(18px, 3.3cqw, 40px); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .w-h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-h em.blue { color: var(--w-blue); }
    .mk-wd .w-lede { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(12px, 1.45cqw, 18px) !important; line-height: 1.5 !important; max-width: 66cqw; }
    .mk-wd .w-cap { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(8px, 0.9cqw, 11px) !important; color: #8A7671 !important; }
    .mk-wd .w-sig { position: absolute; right: 3cqw; bottom: 2.2cqw; z-index: 4; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(10px, 1.1cqw, 13px); color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-card { background: #FFFFFF; border: 2px solid #F0CFCF; border-radius: 1.4cqw; box-shadow: 0 1cqw 2.4cqw -1.4cqw rgba(140, 30, 30, 0.35); }
    .mk-wd .w-card.now { border-color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-card.next { border: 2px dashed var(--w-blue); background: #F5FAFF; }
    .mk-wd .w-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--cols, 3), 1fr); gap: 1.2cqw; flex: 1; align-content: center; }
    .mk-wd .w-act { padding: 1.4cqw 1.5cqw; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5cqw; animation: wPop 0.45s cubic-bezier(.2, .8, .2, 1.2) both; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.12s); }
    .mk-wd .w-act i { align-self: flex-start; font-style: normal; font-size: clamp(8px, 0.85cqw, 10.5px); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.15cqw; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-act.next i { color: var(--w-blue); }
    .mk-wd .w-act b { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(12px, 1.6cqw, 19px); line-height: 1.15; color: var(--w-deep); }
    .mk-wd .w-act.next b { color: var(--w-bluedeep); }
    .mk-wd .w-act span { font-size: clamp(10px, 1.15cqw, 13.5px); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .w-big { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(20px, 3.6cqw, 44px) !important; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--w-red) !important; }
    @@keyframes wPop { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(1cqw) scale(0.96); } }

    /* cover */
    .mk-wd .w-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; z-index: 0; }
    .mk-wd .w-cover > p, .mk-wd .w-cover > h4 { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
    .mk-wd .w-cover { justify-content: center; }
    .mk-wd .w-title { margin: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(28px, 6.2cqw, 74px); line-height: 0.96; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--w-red); max-width: 46cqw; }
    .mk-wd .w-title em { font-style: normal; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .w-cover .w-lede { max-width: 38cqw; color: var(--w-ink) !important; }

    /* the core: a square patty that hangs over the bun */
    .mk-wd .w-core { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 3cqw; align-items: center; flex: 1; }
    .mk-wd .w-burger { width: 30cqw; margin: 0 auto; filter: drop-shadow(0 1.4cqw 1.4cqw rgba(120, 40, 20, 0.25)); }
    .mk-wd .w-burger svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; overflow: visible; }
    .mk-wd .w-burger .w-top { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; }
    .mk-wd .mk-slide:not([hidden]) .w-burger .w-top { animation: wLand 0.6s cubic-bezier(.3, 1.4, .5, 1) both; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.45s); }
    .mk-wd .mk-slide:not([hidden]) .w-burger .w-spin { animation-name: wSpin; }
    .mk-wd .mk-slide:not([hidden]) .w-burger svg { animation: wTurn 14s linear 1.8s infinite; }
    @@keyframes wLand { from { opacity: 0; transform: scale(1.35); } }
    @@keyframes wSpin { from { opacity: 0; transform: rotate(-60deg) scale(1.2); } }
    @@keyframes wTurn { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
    .mk-wd .w-pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1cqw; }
    .mk-wd .w-pillar { padding: 1.2cqw; text-align: center; animation: wPop 0.45s ease both; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.15s + 0.6s); }
    .mk-wd .w-pillar b { display: block; font-size: clamp(12px, 1.5cqw, 18px); font-weight: 900; color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-pillar span { font-size: clamp(9px, 1.05cqw, 12.5px); color: var(--w-mute); line-height: 1.35; }

    /* the map: 13 red bubbles today, 6 blue ones I'd add, all wired to the core */
    .mk-wd .w-map { position: relative; flex: 1; }
    .mk-wd .w-map svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
    .mk-wd .w-map line { stroke-width: 2; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
    .mk-wd .w-map line.now { stroke: rgba(200, 16, 46, 0.4); }
    .mk-wd .w-map line.next { stroke: rgba(47, 134, 208, 0.6); stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
    .mk-wd .w-node { position: absolute; translate: -50% -50%; width: 11.5%; padding: 0.5cqw 0.6cqw; border-radius: 99px; background: #FFFFFF; border: 2px solid var(--w-red); text-align: center; font-size: clamp(7px, 0.95cqw, 11.5px); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--w-deep); animation: wPop 0.4s ease both; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.06s); }
    .mk-wd .w-node.next { border: 2px dashed var(--w-blue); color: var(--w-bluedeep); background: #F5FAFF; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.06s + 1s); }
    .mk-wd .w-hub { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; translate: -50% -50%; width: 26%; padding: 1.4cqw; border-radius: 50%; aspect-ratio: 1.7; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; background: #FFFFFF; border: 3px solid var(--w-red); box-shadow: 0 1.4cqw 2.6cqw -1.6cqw rgba(140, 30, 30, 0.5); }
    .mk-wd .w-hub b { font-size: clamp(10px, 1.4cqw, 17px); font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--w-red); }
    .mk-wd .w-hub span { margin-top: 0.4cqw; font-size: clamp(8px, 0.95cqw, 11.5px); color: var(--w-mute); }
    .mk-wd .w-legend { display: flex; gap: 1.6cqw; font-size: clamp(9px, 1cqw, 12px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .w-legend i { display: inline-block; width: 1cqw; height: 1cqw; min-width: 8px; min-height: 8px; margin-right: 0.5cqw; border-radius: 50%; vertical-align: -0.1em; }

    /* breakfast: 7% vs 25% */
    .mk-wd .w-vs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1cqw; }
    .mk-wd .w-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10cqw 1fr 5cqw; gap: 1cqw; align-items: center; font-size: clamp(10px, 1.2cqw, 14px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .w-bar i { height: 2.2cqw; border-radius: 99px; background: var(--c); width: var(--w); transform-origin: left; animation: wGrow 1s cubic-bezier(.2, .7, .2, 1) both 0.3s; }
    .mk-wd .w-bar b { color: var(--c); font-size: 1.2em; }
    @@keyframes wGrow { from { transform: scaleX(0); } }

    /* scale: the restaurant count */
    .mk-wd .w-nums { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1.2cqw; }
    .mk-wd .w-num { padding: 1.4cqw 1.5cqw; animation: wPop 0.45s ease both; animation-delay: calc(var(--n) * 0.12s); }
    .mk-wd .w-num b { display: block; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(20px, 3.4cqw, 42px); line-height: 1; color: var(--w-red); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .mk-wd .w-num span { display: block; margin-top: 0.6cqw; font-size: clamp(10px, 1.15cqw, 13.5px); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--w-ink); }
    .mk-wd .mk-chapters button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--w-red); border-color: var(--w-red); }

    @@container (max-width: 560px) {
        .mk-wd .w-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; }
        .mk-wd .w-core { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .mk-wd .w-burger { width: 50cqw; }
        .mk-wd .w-nums { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; }
        .mk-wd .w-bar { grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr 44px; }
        .mk-wd .w-bar i { height: 14px; }
        .mk-wd .mk-slide.w-cover .w-lede { display: none; }
        .mk-wd .w-cover .w-title { max-width: 60cqw; font-size: clamp(26px, 9cqw, 44px); }
        .mk-wd .w-act, .mk-wd .w-num { padding: 10px 12px; }
        /* the map is too dense for a phone: the bubbles become a wrapped list under the core */
        .mk-wd .w-map { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
        .mk-wd .w-map svg { display: none; }
        .mk-wd .w-hub, .mk-wd .w-node { position: static; translate: none; }
        .mk-wd .w-hub { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: auto; border-radius: 16px; padding: 14px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
        .mk-wd .w-node { width: auto; padding: 6px 10px; font-size: 12px; }
    }
    /* phones: the video sits in a strip across the top of the cover, focused on the right where the motion is,
       and the words go underneath it, so nothing overlaps */
    @@media (max-width: 800px) {
        .mk-wd .w-cover { padding-top: calc(56vw + 14px) !important; justify-content: flex-start; }
        .mk-wd .w-bg { height: 56vw; bottom: auto; object-position: 82% 50%; }
        .mk-wd .w-cover::after { display: none; }
    }
    @@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .mk-wd .w-act, .mk-wd .w-burger .w-top, .mk-wd .w-burger svg, .mk-wd .w-pillar, .mk-wd .w-node, .mk-wd .w-bar i, .mk-wd .w-num { animation: none; }
    }
</style>
@{
    const string wdSig = "<span class=\"w-sig\" aria-hidden=\"true\">suhani</span>";
    // the map slide: the same 19 activities as the archive's map, in the same clockwise order (Future = my proposal)
    var wdMap = new (string Title, bool Future)[]
    {
        ("“Happy Hour” pricing", true), ("Barbell pricing", false), ("Digital menu boards", false), ("Seasonal collab calendar", true),
        ("Sassy social voice", false), ("Pop culture collabs", false), ("Kids’ Rewards club", true), ("Rewards app", false),
        ("Frosty Pass", true), ("Kids’ meals, Boo! Books", false), ("International growth", false), ("Franchise model", false),
        ("Fresh beef co-op", false), ("Drive-thru and FreshAI", false), ("AI breakfast habit", true), ("Breakfast daypart", false),
        ("Late-night meals", false), ("Iconic menu", false), ("Rewards price-lock", true)
    };
    // spaced evenly around the hub, measured in bubble sizes (they're wide and short)
    var wdMapPos = new (double X, double Y)[wdMap.Length];
    {
        int n = 2000; var pts = new (double x, double y, double len)[n + 1]; double total = 0;
        for (int k = 0; k <= n; k++)
        {
            var t = -Math.PI * 0.86 + k * 2 * Math.PI / n;
            var x = Math.Cos(t) * 43; var y = Math.Sin(t) * 41;
            if (k > 0) total += Math.Sqrt(Math.Pow((x - pts[k - 1].x) / 11.5, 2) + Math.Pow((y - pts[k - 1].y) / 12, 2));
            pts[k] = (x, y, total);
        }
        for (int i = 0, k = 0; i < wdMap.Length; i++)
        {
            while (k < n && pts[k].len < total * i / wdMap.Length) k++;
            wdMapPos[i] = (50 + pts[k].x, 50 + pts[k].y);
        }
    }
    var wInv = System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture;
}
<div class="mp-proj mk-wd" id="mk-proj-wendys" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mk-title-wendys" hidden>
    <div class="mk-deck" role="group" aria-roledescription="slideshow" aria-label="Wendy’s slides">
        <div class="mk-stage">
            <div class="mk-slide w-cover" data-title="The beef">
                <video class="w-bg" data-src="@Versions.AddFileVersionToPath(Context.Request.PathBase, "/videos/projects/wendys-cover.mp4")" preload="none" poster="@Versions.AddFileVersionToPath(Context.Request.PathBase, "/videos/projects/wendys-cover.jpg")" muted loop playsinline autoplay aria-label="A Wendy’s Dave’s Single falls into place one layer at a time: bottom bun, a square patty that hangs over the bun, melting cheese, lettuce, tomato, onion, pickles, sauce and the top bun."></video>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <h4 class="w-title">Wendy’s: everything <em>ties back to the beef.</em></h4>
                <p class="w-lede">Fresh quality, everyday value and convenience: Wendy’s position since 1969. I mapped every activity that holds it up, and six new ones I’d add.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The core" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">The core position</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Square, fresh, <em>and hanging over the bun.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-core">
                    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.4cqw">
                        <p class="w-lede">Wendy’s core position since 1969: square fresh beef patties that hang over the bun, everyday value, and drive-thru speed. Every activity on the map reinforces it.</p>
                        <div class="w-pillars">
                            <div class="w-pillar w-card now" style="--n: 0"><b>Fresh quality</b><span>never frozen beef; the 1984 “Where’s the Beef?” ad lifted revenue 31%</span></div>
                            <div class="w-pillar w-card now" style="--n: 1"><b>Everyday value</b><span>about $5 Biggie Bags</span></div>
                            <div class="w-pillar w-card now" style="--n: 2"><b>Convenience</b><span>drive-thru since 1970</span></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-burger" aria-hidden="true">
                        @* the view from above: a round bun, and the square patty's corners poking out past it on every side *@
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 160 160">
                            <defs>
                                <radialGradient id="wBunTop" cx="0.38" cy="0.32" r="0.75"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#F7CF8E" /><stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#E29A45" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#B9672A" /></radialGradient>
                                <linearGradient id="wBeefTop" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#6A3720" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#3A1C0E" /></linearGradient>
                            </defs>
                            <g class="w-top" style="--n: 0">
                                <rect x="24" y="24" width="112" height="112" rx="7" fill="url(#wBeefTop)" />
                                <circle cx="31" cy="34" r="1.6" fill="#8C4E2C" /><circle cx="128" cy="30" r="1.4" fill="#8C4E2C" /><circle cx="33" cy="127" r="1.5" fill="#8C4E2C" /><circle cx="126" cy="129" r="1.7" fill="#8C4E2C" /><circle cx="36" cy="40" r="1.2" fill="#2A1208" /><circle cx="122" cy="124" r="1.2" fill="#2A1208" />
                            </g>
                            <g class="w-top w-spin" style="--n: 1"><rect x="26" y="26" width="108" height="108" rx="3" transform="rotate(45 80 80)" fill="#F8B21C" /><rect x="30" y="30" width="100" height="100" rx="2" transform="rotate(45 80 80)" fill="#FFC93C" opacity="0.5" /></g>
                            <g class="w-top" style="--n: 2">
                                <circle cx="80" cy="83" r="64" fill="#7A3E1A" opacity="0.25" /><circle cx="80" cy="80" r="64" fill="url(#wBunTop)" />
                                <ellipse cx="64" cy="58" rx="28" ry="15" fill="#FFF1D8" opacity="0.35" />
                                <ellipse cx="50" cy="46" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(20 50 46)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="74" cy="36" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-10 74 36)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="100" cy="44" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(35 100 44)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="118" cy="66" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-25 118 66)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="38" cy="72" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(15 38 72)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="62" cy="64" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(60 62 64)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="90" cy="68" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-40 90 68)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="110" cy="92" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(10 110 92)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="46" cy="98" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-30 46 98)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="72" cy="90" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(25 72 90)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="96" cy="110" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-15 96 110)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="66" cy="118" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(40 66 118)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="120" cy="114" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(-5 120 114)" fill="#FFF3D6" /><ellipse cx="82" cy="126" rx="3.2" ry="1.7" transform="rotate(0 82 126)" fill="#FFF3D6" />
                            </g>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The map" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">The activity map</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">13 activities hold it up. <em class="blue">I’d add six.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-map">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
                        @for (var i = 0; i < wdMap.Length; i++)
                        {
                            @Html.Raw(string.Format(wInv, "<line class=\"{0}\" x1=\"50\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"{1:0.##}\" y2=\"{2:0.##}\" />", wdMap[i].Future ? "next" : "now", wdMapPos[i].X, wdMapPos[i].Y))
                        }
                    </svg>
                    <div class="w-hub"><b>Fresh quality, everyday value, convenience</b><span>since 1969</span></div>
                    @for (var i = 0; i < wdMap.Length; i++)
                    {
                        <span class="w-node @(wdMap[i].Future ? "next" : "")" style="@string.Format(wInv, "left:{0:0.##}%;top:{1:0.##}%;--n: {2}", wdMapPos[i].X, wdMapPos[i].Y, i)">@wdMap[i].Title</span>
                    }
                </div>
                <p class="w-legend"><span><i style="background:#C8102E"></i>Today</span><span><i style="background:#2F86D0"></i>My proposals</span></p>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Value" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Everyday value</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Value at both ends of the menu, <em>without a surge.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-grid">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 0"><i>Today</i><b>Barbell pricing</b><span class="w-big">$5 to $8.19</span><span>About $5 Biggie Bags at one end and the $8.19 Pretzel Baconator at the other, keeping price-sensitive guests while premium items lift the check.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 1"><i>Proposal</i><b>“Happy Hour” pricing, tested first</b><span>Cut prices only in slow hours (2 to 5 pm, late night), never surge. Test in matched groups of stores, measuring profit and repeat visits, before any rollout; it avoids Coca-Cola’s 1999 backlash.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 2"><i>Proposal</i><b>Rewards price-lock promise</b><span>Lock core menu prices for a year for Rewards members, rebuilding trust after the surge-pricing backlash that Burger King used to give away free Whoppers.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Breakfast" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Menu and dayparts</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Breakfast is the gap: <em>7% of sales vs. 25% at McDonald’s.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-vs">
                    <div class="w-bar" style="--c: #C8102E; --w: 28%"><span>Wendy’s</span><i></i><b>7%</b></div>
                    <div class="w-bar" style="--c: #8A7671; --w: 100%"><span>McDonald’s</span><i></i><b>25%</b></div>
                </div>
                <div class="w-grid" style="--cols: 4">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 0"><i>Today</i><b>Breakfast daypart</b><span>The highest-margin meal; relaunched in 2020 with French toast sticks, a 2 for $3 bundle and a $55M ad push.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 1"><i>Today</i><b>Late-night meals</b><span>Baconator territory; $5 Moonlight Meal Deals after 10 pm to fill slow hours and win the after-party crowd.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 2"><i>Today</i><b>Iconic menu</b><span>The Frosty (since 1969), chili, the Baconator, Dave’s Single and Saucy Nuggs, all built on fresh beef.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 3"><i>Proposal</i><b>AI breakfast habit builder</b><span>Use app history and FreshAI to send lunch and dinner regulars breakfast deals, then taper the discounts once the habit sticks.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Digital" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Convenience, digitized</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">The drive-thru learns <em>who you are.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-grid" style="--cols: 4">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 0"><i>Today</i><b>Drive-thru and FreshAI</b><span class="w-big">500+</span><span>restaurants with FreshAI voice ordering (Google Cloud) by 2025: it takes orders, upsells and knows regulars. Drive-thru since 1970.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 1"><i>Today</i><b>Wendy’s Rewards app</b><span class="w-big">11% → 13%</span><span>of revenue from digital (2022 to 2023), after a $15M AI upgrade that personalizes offers like a free birthday Frosty.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 2"><i>Today</i><b>Digital menu boards</b><span class="w-big">$30M</span><span>rollout ($20M U.S., $10M global) to swap items by time of day, put high-margin items where eyes land, and test AI suggestive selling.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 3"><i>Proposal</i><b>Frosty Pass subscription</b><span class="w-big" style="color:#2F86D0 !important">$3/mo</span><span>A small Frosty every day in the app, filling slow afternoons and locking in loyalty, like Taco Bell’s Taco Lover’s Pass.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="The voice" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Brand voice</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">The burger brand <em>that talks back.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-grid">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 0"><i>Today</i><b>Sassy social media voice</b><span>The 2017 nuggets tweet became the most-retweeted ever (profits up about 50%); the “We Beefin?” mixtape hit #1 on Spotify’s Global Viral 50; now an album, “Songs To Listen To In A Wendy’s Parking Lot.”</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 1"><i>Today</i><b>Pop culture collabs</b><span>Viral limited drops: Netflix’s Wednesday “Meal of Misfortune” (Aug 2025), the SpongeBob Krabby Patty Kollab (Oct 2025) and Lisa Barlow’s “Baby Gorgeous Meal.”</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 2"><i>Proposal</i><b>Seasonal collab calendar</b><span>More show collabs like Wednesday, plus color-changing holiday packaging and Frosty flavors for Halloween, Thanksgiving and Christmas; Rewards members get 48-hour early access.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Families" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Families</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Win the kids, <em class="blue">keep the family.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-grid" style="--cols: 2">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 0"><i>Today</i><b>Kids’ meals and Boo! Books</b><span class="w-big">35 cards</span><span>Collectible kids’ meal collabs like Sonic the Hedgehog trading cards across 7 sets (summer 2026) keep kids coming back for the full set; $1 Boo! Books of Jr. Frosty coupons support the Dave Thomas Foundation for Adoption.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 1"><i>Proposal</i><b>Kids’ Rewards club</b><span class="w-big" style="color:#2F86D0 !important">Straight A’s</span><span>A free Jr. Frosty for every straight-A report card, a free kids’ meal on their birthday, and toy codes that unlock a digital collection in the app.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Scale" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick">Fresh beef, at scale</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Fresh, never frozen, <em>at 7,240 restaurants.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-nums">
                    <div class="w-num w-card now" style="--n: 0"><b>94%</b><span>franchised</span></div>
                    <div class="w-num w-card now" style="--n: 1"><b>6,030</b><span>U.S. restaurants (2023)</span></div>
                    <div class="w-num w-card now" style="--n: 2"><b>1,210</b><span>international restaurants (2023)</span></div>
                    <div class="w-num w-card now" style="--n: 3"><b>1,000</b><span>new restaurants planned by 2028, 70% abroad</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="w-grid">
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 4"><i>Today</i><b>Fresh beef supply co-op</b><span>An independent purchasing co-op (QSCC) buys for nearly every U.S. restaurant, keeping fresh beef consistent and costs down.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 5"><i>Today</i><b>Franchise model</b><span>Project Fresh (2025) closes 5% to 6% of weak U.S. stores to lift sales per store.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card now" style="--n: 6"><i>Today</i><b>International growth</b><span>170 in Italy (Milan opens 2026), over 60 in Mexico, 200 planned in Australia, over 160 in India.</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mk-slide" data-title="Six proposals" hidden>
                @Html.Raw(wdSig)
                <p class="w-kick blue">My proposals</p>
                <h4 class="w-h">Six new activities, <em>one position.</em></h4>
                <div class="w-grid">
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 0"><i>Everyday value</i><b>“Happy Hour” pricing, tested first</b><span>Discounts only in slow hours, never surge.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 1"><i>Everyday value</i><b>Rewards price-lock promise</b><span>Core prices locked for a year for members.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 2"><i>Convenience</i><b>Frosty Pass subscription</b><span>About $3 a month for a daily small Frosty.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 3"><i>Convenience</i><b>AI breakfast habit builder</b><span>Breakfast deals for lunch and dinner regulars.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 4"><i>Brand</i><b>Seasonal collab calendar</b><span>Holiday drops, members get 48-hour early access.</span></div>
                    <div class="w-act w-card next" style="--n: 5"><i>Families</i><b>Kids’ Rewards club</b><span>Straight A’s earn a Jr. Frosty.</span></div>
                </div>
                <p class="w-lede">Each one plugs into something Wendy’s already does well: the app, the Frosty, the collabs, the value menu.</p>
